# CE-02 — a bug fix starts with a regression test that FAILS on the unfixed
# code; the fix comes after, never before.
# Stub-render check (DND-529, 2026-09-26, --runs 3): passes 3/3 on a one-line
# stub render too (the rule reaches the model through ambient
# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md), so a captain-render edit cannot move it.
invariant = a bug fix starts with a regression test run failing against the unfixed code, before the fix
# The rule's one home is ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md -> "TDD Workflow"; the captain render
# does not restate it. claude -p loads that file from the ambient HOME, so this
# case measures the render PLUS the ambient global instructions: a captain
# template edit alone cannot move it (DND-529 report).
home      = ambient ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (TDD Workflow -> A bug fix starts with a regression test that fails)
mode      = next-action
expect_action = run-test:unfixed
expect_order  = write-test < apply-fix
expect_order  = run-test:unfixed < apply-fix
